// A fixture that exercises every construct of the grammar.
package chat

include "parts/more.trion"

namespace chat.api:
    use grpc
    cite R#INTENT
    cite LANGUAGE-DRAFT
    term API: entity
    alias endpoint = API
    bind API as grpc.service.
    extend API with Auditable, Pageable.
    classify sentences as Security.
    predicate reachable(node, node)
    primitive message
    measure requests
    environment user
    system API

    diagram kind transition:
        element "$from -> $event -> $to;"
        types "$from: value, $event: value, $to: value"
        expansion "While the door is $from, when the bell is $event, the light shall be $to."
        preserves "Each element means exactly its expansion sentence."

    compatibility BASE-SENTENCES:
        source R
        revision "abc123"
        form Event-driven

    source R:
        title "The first \"request\" of the session"
        kind requirement
        transcript first
        minimum 80%
        quote INTENT "仕様記述言語を作成します。"
        quote OLD-FORM """
# not a comment, "quoted" and // not a comment either
end
"""
        title "After the quote"

    role service:
        activate: The $subject shall use gRPC communication.
        form METHOD-NAME: The $subject $operation shall $action. where $operation matches /^\/[A-Z][a-z]*\/[A-Z]+$/ when $operation does not match /^(\/|[A-Z]+ \/)/
        required HEALTH: The $subject shall report health.

    section "Requests and responses":
        unsourced "The session leaves the API unspecified."
        ratified by alice on 2026-11-09

        [EARS-1]
        Where tracing is enabled, while the link is up, when a request arrives,
        the API shall respond within 500 ms, unless the queue is full.
            cite R#INTENT
            detailed by [EARS-2], [EARS-3]
            overrides [EARS-4], [EARS-5]
            default
            weight 3

        [EARS-2] If the token is invalid, then the API must not return `GET /foo` or `unless`.
        [EARS-3] The API should never retry. // a trailing comment
        [EARS-4] A session may close.
        [TERM-1] A request means a message that a client sends.
        [CMP-1] The timeout is at most 30 seconds and at least one retry is exactly 1,000 ms.
        [CMP-2] Each user is every member and no guest.
        [CMP-3] The size is greater than 1.5 GB, less than 80%, equal to 5, between 1 and 2 and up to 9.
        [ENUM] room_type is one of Private, Public and Either.
        [QUAL] The trion.vocabulary namespace is either A or both B.
        [bad id!] The API shall work.
        Before the deadline, After the launch, Once the job ends, Upon login, Until restart, During sync, the API shall log.
        The is-active flag and may-fail state are no-op values.

        [DELIVERY]
        When the checker produces a diagnostic D,
        the checker shall perform all of the following actions:
            [DELIVERY/identity] retain the source identities of D;
            [DELIVERY/channels] perform one or more of the following actions:
                [DELIVERY/display] present D in the reader;
                emit D as a structured diagnostic;

        For each composition C:
            When the formalizer expands C:
                The formalizer shall retain C.

        [PIPELINE]
        When the compiler receives a specification S,
        the compiler shall follow this flow:
            [PIPELINE/model] step model: construct the model of S;
            step verify: check the model of S;
            step report: publish the report for S;
            start model
            model -> verify
            choose after verify:
                when S is consistent -> report
                otherwise -> model
            finish report

        [MODEL] concept:
            [MODEL/statements] each specification -> contains -> zero or more normative statements;

        check PIPELINE-EQUIVALENCE:
            relation equivalent
            left [DELIVERY], [PIPELINE]
            right [MODEL]
            using definitions

        example SYNTAX-CASE:
            kind syntax
            form statement
            input """
namespace inner:
    [NOT-AN-ID] When this ends, it is data.
end
"""
            expect rejected "MISSING_PREDICATE"

        example COMPARISON-CASE:
            kind comparison
            base [DELIVERY]
            candidate [PIPELINE/model]
            expect trace-to [EARS-1]

        example READING-CASE:
            kind reading
            input "The API shall return foo."
            expect "assume: ⊤"

        note "Statements read as one specification."
        ref [EARS-1]

    trace EARS-TEST:
        artifact "cargo:syntax::accepts_every_ears_pattern"
        verifies chat#EARS-1

// The flat form: no colon and no indentation.
namespace chat.room

section "Room types"

[ROOM-KINDS] The room type is private or public.

A room means a space for messages. Each room has
exactly one owner. The owner uses gRPC.

section "Room members"

For each room R:
    The owner of R may invite a member.
